<!--MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.StatusConvention-->
<concept:StatusConvention xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:status="org.blockml.bml.status">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A guide to MachineBlocks status Block references
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Maturity is expressed with Status Block references — not free strings or boolean flags.
    
    Core status blocks (package org.blockml.bml.status.*):
    Stable — implemented, tested, and mapping complete; reliable behaviour (implicit default).
    Draft — definition exists; implementation or mapping incomplete, untested, or
      intentionally divergent; may change.
    Stub — placeholder; shape declared, behaviour not yet specified; validates OK;
      renderer may stub/log or abort.
    Deprecated — retained for compatibility; do not use in new work.
    
    Default is Stable. Status inherits downward; authors declare status only when diverging from
    the inherited effective status.
    
    At &lt;status> and bml:status reference sites, unqualified names resolve to
    org.blockml.bml.status.* — bare names are correct there
    (e.g. &lt;status>Draft&lt;/status>, bml:status="Deprecated").
    Explicit prefixes or FQNs remain valid everywhere (status:Draft ≡ Draft at those sites).
    Bare status names are invalid outside specialized status reference sites.
    
    SCAD implementation status and MBOM mapping status may differ independently for the same
    parameter or type. Use Draft with an explicit note when they are misaligned.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="concept:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso">
      Start of the concept reading path.
    </see>
    <see type="status:Stable" relation="Defines">
      Default maturity status.
    </see>
    <see type="status:Draft" relation="Defines">
      Incomplete or untested work status.
    </see>
    <see type="status:Stub" relation="Defines">
      Placeholder status.
    </see>
    <see type="status:Deprecated" relation="Defines">
      Compatibility-only status.
    </see>
    <see file="docs/02_mbml.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      BlockML status authoring rules.
    </see>
  </references>
</concept:StatusConvention>
